title: A save says what it hides and stops hiding, and why a child that left a subscriber hid nothing. Since 2026-11-14.
pid: b4114760-8249-499c-862a-6a458074bbb5
body: |2-
  No edit shows a hide: the server infers it from what left a
  subscriber. So a gesture that hid nothing looked like one that worked,
  as Top found twice on 2026-11-14. Now the save's answer carries one
  line per hide and unhide its plan writes ("Hides 'X' from 'C', as
  content of 'N'."), and one per child that left an owned subscriber
  that subscribes to something without hiding anything, naming the
  rule that held ("Hides nothing: 'R' left 'C', but it is no content of
  'N', nor overrides any."). The lines compare each subscriber the plan
  writes with the graph, not the inference's steps, so every source of
  a hide is reported ('hide_report_lines' in
  'server/from_text/hide_report.rs'). Emacs and Neovim show them after
  the save; the AI reader also before it, by a preview: a save request
  that stops once the plan is checked, and writes nothing. Each choice
  made for Jeff, the other way, and what is not reported:
  [[id:41d36710-9473-4b9e-b7aa-648c5cd8f7c9][the hide report as built: each choice, why, and which were Jeff's]].
